<title>MALAYSIA: Tekala says negotiating to buy assets.</title>
<headline>Tekala says negotiating to buy assets.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian timber firm Tekala Corp Bhd said it was in the final stage of negotiations to buy &quot;certain assets&quot;.</p>
<p>It did not give other details in its statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange late on Tuesday, but said an announcement would be made within five market days.</p>
<p>The statement was made following the suspension of its stock from trading from June 25. The stock was last traded at 5.20 ringgit.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
